# The Desktop's system functions (DESK=1; tests/mousegen.py makes tests/system.keys from this).
# The card gets its own /SYSTEM/PROGRAMS (PREP in the Makefile): Terminal, Paint, Edit, a
# missing program (left out of the menu) and HELLO. Shots (s), total 57 s:
#   6.3   the Programs menu read from /SYSTEM/PROGRAMS (no "Missing": its program is not there)
#   11    the Terminal: "hog 1 &" holds all memory but a bank; "hello": the shell's message
#   13    Programs > Paint: "Not enough memory to start Paint. Close a program and try again."
#   15.5  Horizon > Force quit...: the running programs, End: HOG selected
#   18.5  Enter: HOG killed (memory back in the status); About Horizon
#   21.5  the Terminal clicked (over About), About again: the same About raised (one instance)
#   28.5  Edit with "hello" typed; Horizon > Shut down...: the confirmation
#   31    Enter: Files and the Terminal closed; Edit asks to save
#   34    Esc (Cancel): "Edit did not close. Nothing was stopped."
#   37.5  OK; Shut down again: Edit asks again
#   42    Discard: "It is now safe to switch off the Atari816." (SYS_SYNC)
#   46    Restart clicked (SYS_RESTART 1): Horizon starts again (the pointer then goes to the
#         top left corner: the new kernel starts it at the centre)
#   49    README.TXT dragged from Files onto the desktop with Shift: moved into /Desktop, its
#         icon (0.14: without Shift a shortcut)
#   52    the SD card icon double clicked: Files at the root
#   56    the README.TXT icon (where it was dropped) double clicked: Edit with it
5600 move 105 8
5700 click
